{
  "bridge_text": "The firefly's faint light flickers in the shadows of the moss, waiting for the help Mosk was once too afraid to bring. We shall see if they can mend that old hurt together.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "The poor firefly lay so still on her bed of moss, her light dimming like a candle in a draft. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he remembered that long-ago winter when his courage failed him. He had guarded this hollow tree through every season since, hoping for a chance to make things right, though his heart remained heavy with the memory of that lost medicine."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt softly and asked the firefly queen what she needed to feel strong again. A drop of warm milk and a kind word, the queen breathed, for that was all medicine ever truly was. Mosk hurried to fetch the milk in a tiny thimble, laying his paw gently beside hers. As the queen’s glow steadied, the humming inside the tree blossomed into a new, beautiful tune, and Mosk, for the first time in years, hummed along."
    }
  ],
